			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I’ve had the pleasure of working with the group organizing Cincinnati Day of Agile.&#160; About a week ago we confirm our facility and date: March 26th, 2011 at the <a href="http://savannahcenter.com">Savanna Center</a> in West Chester, Ohio.&#160; We expect quite a jump this year, going over 300 attendees.</p>
<p>We are currently accepting topics for both the Beginner and Advanced tracks.&#160; If you have any experiences with Agile techniques either good, bad or wild this is your chance to help others learn from those experiences.&#160; Whether it’s the impact of a transparent backlog on your business, the passionate arguments that came from a collaborating team, or the impact of coding practices on your velocity over time, people want to know what you have to say.&#160; Don’t be shy.&#160; Submit your topics at <a href="http://cincydayofagile.org">http://cincydayofagile.org</a> soon!</p>
<p>&#160;</p>
<p>Looks forward to seeing everyone there.&#160; The facility is beautiful and the discussions are going to be awesome, so don’t miss out. </p>
]]></content:encoded>
